# Generated output
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
/tmp
/output/

# Runtime artifacts (training runs, persisted state, logs)
**/output/
*.jsonl
*.bin
*.csv

# General test/run byproducts (must never be tracked)
*.aof
*.pcap
*.log
*.out
*.profraw
*.profdata

# IDE / editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS garbage
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Debug output
l9_debug.txt
**/l9_debug.txt

# Cargo build artifacts (non-standard)
**/target/

# Evidence: verification corpus stays local, not in git
#
# The evidence/ tree (E01–E124 contracts, probes, results) is the project's
# verification corpus. Per evidence/README.md it must be preserved locally,
# but it is deliberately NOT tracked by git: probes and build artifacts are
# regenerable verification noise, and keeping the whole tree out of the
# repository keeps it focused on the crate itself. The contracts
# (evidence/README.md, evidence/contracts.md) describe what was verified and
# how to re-run the probes.
/evidence/

# Internal design workspace (I1 layer): local working notes, not public
# documentation. Per docs/doc-governance.md, the I1 tier records design-time
# decisions in Chinese; it is not part of the published documentation and is
# deliberately NOT tracked by git.
/docs/internal/*
# Exception: the theory corpus IS tracked (prevention of loss of the
# foundational documents): meta-foundations.md, boundary-ontology.md,
# frontier-notes.md, and the history archive.
!/docs/internal/theory/

# Reasonix desktop session metadata (local tool state)
.reasonix/
world_events.log
redis_like.aof
packets.pcap

redis_like_aof_writer_*.aof
reasonix.toml

# Node.js / TypeScript tooling (used for ad-hoc blueprint TS workflows; not part
# of the Rust crate). Node_modules and lockfiles would otherwise pollute the repo.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
*.tsbuildinfo

